    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d814">

                <pb facs="0962" n="868" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg868"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-09-30"><hi rendition="#italic">September 30,
                        1896</hi></date>. (Received Oct. 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1005.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Sir: I have the honor to inclose a copy of a letter from President Tracy, of
                    Marsovan College, which shows that orders have been issued for the security of
                    the people there.</p>
                <p>His anxiety for a more liberal iradé for his college is natural, but just now
                    such matters would receive no attention.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d814-a1.xml" xpointer="d814-a1"/>
